WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:03.799
Is your inbox overflowing with emails?

1
00:00:04.769 --> 00:00:05.750
You're not alone.

2
00:00:06.329 --> 00:00:07.079
Hey everyone,

3
00:00:07.369 --> 00:00:08.069
Kevin here.

4
00:00:08.489 --> 00:00:08.850
Today,

5
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.109
I'll show you one of the best ways to take control

6
00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:16.149
of your Outlook inbox and finally hit inbox 0.

7
00:00:16.569 --> 00:00:19.670
I used this exact system when I worked at Microsoft,

8
00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:24.350
and it made a huge difference in staying organized and on top of my work.

9
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:25.989
Let's dive in.

10
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.559
Here I am in my Outlook inbox,

11
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.329
using Outlook on the web.

12
00:00:30.559 --> 00:00:32.229
If you're using the desktop app,

13
00:00:32.479 --> 00:00:33.080
no worries,

14
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.240
the same system works there too.

15
00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:36.229
Now,

16
00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:38.430
I have all these different emails in my inbox,

17
00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.569
some of them need just a quick response,

18
00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.060
some will take longer,

19
00:00:42.229 --> 00:00:42.900
some can wait,

20
00:00:42.959 --> 00:00:44.990
and some are just noise.

21
00:00:45.799 --> 00:00:47.240
To organize all of this email,

22
00:00:47.349 --> 00:00:52.180
we're going to use a simple 3-folder system to get through all of this.

23
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.599
Over on the left-hand side,

24
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.180
you'll see that there are some existing folders

25
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.000
that Outlook created for us,

26
00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.979
but we're going to add to this list.

27
00:01:00.439 --> 00:01:00.880
So right here,

28
00:01:00.959 --> 00:01:01.680
we have folders,

29
00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.000
and when we hover over this,

30
00:01:03.119 --> 00:01:05.180
you'll see the three dots over on the right-hand side.

31
00:01:05.599 --> 00:01:06.360
Let's click on this,

32
00:01:06.379 --> 00:01:09.160
and right here we have the option to create a new folder.

33
00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:10.069
Let's click here.

34
00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:12.190
First,

35
00:01:12.309 --> 00:01:14.940
let's create a folder called action items,

36
00:01:15.029 --> 00:01:15.370
and

37
00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:19.650
this will contain all of the different emails that you need to respond to or act on.

38
00:01:19.989 --> 00:01:21.069
Once you've finished typing that in,

39
00:01:21.139 --> 00:01:22.110
click on the check mark,

40
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:24.400
and there we now see our new folder.

41
00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:26.139
Let's click on these three dots,

42
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:29.389
and we could change some of the properties related to this folder.

43
00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:29.830
Right here,

44
00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:31.610
we have the option to change the color.

45
00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:32.940
Let's set that to red,

46
00:01:32.949 --> 00:01:34.699
so this folder really stands out.

47
00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.569
We'll be spending a lot of time here.

48
00:01:36.989 --> 00:01:38.190
Let's go back up to folders,

49
00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.470
we see the three dots again,

50
00:01:39.589 --> 00:01:41.910
let's click on this and let's add another new folder.

51
00:01:42.069 --> 00:01:42.889
I'll click here,

52
00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:44.230
and for this folder,

53
00:01:44.319 --> 00:01:46.110
let's call it Waiting on.

54
00:01:46.529 --> 00:01:51.470
This will contain all the messages where we're waiting for someone else to respond.

55
00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:54.269
Sometimes you'll send someone a request and

56
00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:55.129
they don't get back to you,

57
00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.830
in which case you need to ping them again

58
00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.730
or remind them about your email.

59
00:01:59.010 --> 00:01:59.370
Right over here,

60
00:01:59.489 --> 00:02:00.559
let's click on the check mark,

61
00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:01.870
and that adds the folder.

62
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:02.370
Here too,

63
00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.709
let's click on the three dots and let's change the color.

64
00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:05.370
For this one,

65
00:02:05.489 --> 00:02:06.290
I'll go with a,

66
00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.350
let's say a soothing dark green,

67
00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.190
I like that.

68
00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:11.470
And let's click on the three dots again,

69
00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:12.330
next to folders,

70
00:02:12.369 --> 00:02:14.270
and let's add 1 more folder.

71
00:02:14.639 --> 00:02:15.559
And for this one,

72
00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.699
we'll call this Read later.

73
00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:18.940
This will contain

74
00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.940
newsletters or reference materials,

75
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.899
basically FYI's that you'd like to catch up on.

76
00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.190
They're not urgent,

77
00:02:25.199 --> 00:02:27.059
and they don't need your immediate attention.

78
00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:27.880
Right over here,

79
00:02:28.039 --> 00:02:29.000
let's click on the checkmark,

80
00:02:29.199 --> 00:02:30.220
there we see it in the list.

81
00:02:30.479 --> 00:02:31.399
Let's click on the three dots,

82
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:31.839
and here too,

83
00:02:31.919 --> 00:02:33.220
let's also change the color.

84
00:02:33.559 --> 00:02:34.000
For this one,

85
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.139
let's go with a gold color.

86
00:02:36.279 --> 00:02:36.880
Now click on that.

87
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.070
And there we see the color applied.

88
00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.470
Now that we've added these 3 different folders,

89
00:02:41.589 --> 00:02:42.910
we can reorganize them,

90
00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:45.490
so the most important ones are front and center.

91
00:02:45.789 --> 00:02:46.139
Right here,

92
00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.110
I see that inbox is 4th on the list,

93
00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:50.520
but this is where all of my incoming email lands.

94
00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.830
So I'd like this to be at the top of my list.

95
00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:53.830
I'll press and hold,

96
00:02:53.869 --> 00:02:55.649
and here I can drag that right to the top.

97
00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:57.490
Then I have my action items,

98
00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.880
read later and waiting on.

99
00:02:59.000 --> 00:02:59.169
Now,

100
00:02:59.289 --> 00:03:01.899
I'd rather have waiting on ahead of read later.

101
00:03:02.009 --> 00:03:02.320
So here,

102
00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.440
I'll press and hold on this,

103
00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:06.369
and let me put it in between action items and read later,

104
00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:06.990
and there,

105
00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.050
I now have the order that I like using.

106
00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:12.050
Along with the 3 folders that we created,

107
00:03:12.169 --> 00:03:15.210
Outlook also has a number of pre-existing folders,

108
00:03:15.279 --> 00:03:18.229
and we're going to use a few of those in this system.

109
00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:19.250
Right up on top,

110
00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:20.410
we have the inbox,

111
00:03:20.529 --> 00:03:23.009
and this is where all of the incoming email lands.

112
00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:28.240
This is also where we're going to triage all of the email into our different folders.

113
00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.500
We also have another folder called the archive,

114
00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:33.940
and this is where we'll place most of the emails

115
00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.740
after we've handled them or after we've responded to them.

116
00:03:36.979 --> 00:03:40.059
And we also have another folder called the deleted items.

117
00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:43.169
This is typically where I move archived emails,

118
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:44.750
let's say 2 to 3 times a year,

119
00:03:44.929 --> 00:03:48.309
or basically anything that's older than 6 months and I no longer need.

120
00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.869
Now that we've established this structure,

121
00:03:51.009 --> 00:03:53.369
let's go through and let's clean out this inbox together,

122
00:03:53.449 --> 00:03:54.250
and as we do that,

123
00:03:54.369 --> 00:03:55.729
I'll explain the logic

124
00:03:55.949 --> 00:03:58.559
for why we move certain emails into different folders.

125
00:03:58.839 --> 00:03:59.570
Now right up on top,

126
00:03:59.649 --> 00:04:01.169
I have the cookie newsletter,

127
00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.410
and as much as I would love to read it right now,

128
00:04:03.729 --> 00:04:04.809
I just don't have the time,

129
00:04:04.929 --> 00:04:06.710
but it is something I would like to review.

130
00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.630
So let's take this email right here,

131
00:04:08.639 --> 00:04:11.699
and then we can drag it over and place it into read later.

132
00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:13.539
Next up,

133
00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.169
I have an email from Grady,

134
00:04:15.339 --> 00:04:17.100
and he wants to know if I could pull together

135
00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:20.089
a new version of the customer training slide deck.

136
00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.769
This is an action on me,

137
00:04:21.858 --> 00:04:25.649
and it'll also take a little bit of time to pull together this deck.

138
00:04:26.019 --> 00:04:26.309
So,

139
00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.089
I'm going to respond to Grady,

140
00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:31.579
letting him know that I received this message and I'll start working on it,

141
00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:33.959
but it's not something that I could do right now.

142
00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.019
I'll type in my message and right up above,

143
00:04:36.059 --> 00:04:37.019
let's click on send.

144
00:04:37.809 --> 00:04:39.029
Now that I've sent my message,

145
00:04:39.399 --> 00:04:42.790
I need to remember to follow up on this and actually complete the work.

146
00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.450
Let's take the message from Grady,

147
00:04:44.489 --> 00:04:47.109
and here I'll drag it over into action items.

148
00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:48.779
Next up,

149
00:04:48.859 --> 00:04:49.980
I have an email from Pradeep,

150
00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.839
letting me know that my Kevin Cookie Company mugs have shipped.

151
00:04:53.179 --> 00:04:55.579
This email has no action item on me,

152
00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.799
so I can either delete this message right up here,

153
00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:59.279
or we can archive it.

154
00:04:59.500 --> 00:04:59.619
Now,

155
00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:00.980
I like archiving messages,

156
00:05:01.059 --> 00:05:04.079
that way I keep a record of all these different messages.

157
00:05:04.679 --> 00:05:07.859
One shortcut key that you could use to very quickly archive a message on the web,

158
00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.049
simply press the E key on your keyboard,

159
00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.929
or if you're using the desktop client,

160
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.630
you could press the backspace key.

161
00:05:13.739 --> 00:05:14.660
I'll press E,

162
00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.399
and that archives the message.

163
00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:17.660
Next up,

164
00:05:17.739 --> 00:05:18.940
I have an email from Alex,

165
00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:23.040
and it looks like he wants me to pull together key metrics from last quarter.

166
00:05:23.459 --> 00:05:25.019
Now this seems like an action item,

167
00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.959
but I'm actually not the best person on the team to help with this.

168
00:05:28.179 --> 00:05:31.359
Adele is our data analyst and she'd be a much better fit.

169
00:05:31.929 --> 00:05:33.260
Why don't we delegate this to her?

170
00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:33.899
Right up on top,

171
00:05:34.019 --> 00:05:37.380
I'll click on the forward icon and let's type in Adele's name.

172
00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:37.899
Here she is,

173
00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:38.700
Adele Vance,

174
00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:39.700
and right down below,

175
00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.000
I'll type in my message

176
00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.320
and see if she can pull it together.

177
00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:44.220
Now right up on top,

178
00:05:44.339 --> 00:05:45.260
let's click on send.

179
00:05:46.149 --> 00:05:47.910
Now that I've delegated this to Adele,

180
00:05:48.029 --> 00:05:49.549
there's no action on me.

181
00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.239
So let's archive this message.

182
00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.940
I'll press the E key on my keyboard,

183
00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:53.809
and that archives it.

184
00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.049
Next up,

185
00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.890
I have an email from Diego,

186
00:05:56.929 --> 00:05:59.010
and it looks like he has a quick question.

187
00:05:59.170 --> 00:05:59.440
Right here,

188
00:05:59.450 --> 00:05:59.690
he says,

189
00:05:59.739 --> 00:06:02.149
are you still planning to present the Outlook tips section

190
00:06:02.489 --> 00:06:03.970
during Friday's meeting?

191
00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:07.589
If the email response will take under 2 minutes,

192
00:06:07.709 --> 00:06:10.369
I just recommend responding to it right now.

193
00:06:10.619 --> 00:06:11.989
If it'll take longer than that,

194
00:06:12.109 --> 00:06:14.640
then we can move it over to the action items folder.

195
00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:15.390
In this case,

196
00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.850
this is a very quick response,

197
00:06:16.989 --> 00:06:17.510
so over here,

198
00:06:17.619 --> 00:06:18.540
let's click on reply,

199
00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:19.730
I'll type in my response,

200
00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:21.369
and let's send that to Diego.

201
00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:21.790
And there,

202
00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:22.929
I've answered the question,

203
00:06:23.269 --> 00:06:25.170
and there's no additional action on me.

204
00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:25.619
So,

205
00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:27.100
with this message selected,

206
00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.769
let's press E and that archives the message.

207
00:06:30.579 --> 00:06:31.019
Last up,

208
00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.899
I have an email from Patty Fernandez,

209
00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:33.940
my manager,

210
00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:37.250
and it looks like there are some updated packaging designs and she

211
00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.019
would like me to review them and also provide some feedback.

212
00:06:40.579 --> 00:06:42.459
This will definitely take longer than 2 minutes,

213
00:06:42.519 --> 00:06:44.679
in which case I should follow up on this later.

214
00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:45.339
Right up on top,

215
00:06:45.459 --> 00:06:46.640
let's click reply all,

216
00:06:46.709 --> 00:06:48.619
and just let her know that I received the message and

217
00:06:48.619 --> 00:06:50.980
I'll get back with feedback by the end of the week.

218
00:06:51.329 --> 00:06:52.540
Now that I've typed out my message,

219
00:06:52.739 --> 00:06:53.750
I'll send this to Patty,

220
00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.540
but there is a follow-up on me.

221
00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:56.100
So over here,

222
00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.440
I'll take Patty's message

223
00:06:57.579 --> 00:06:59.359
and let's move that over to action items.

224
00:06:59.619 --> 00:07:00.369
And just like that,

225
00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:02.320
we now have inbox 0.

226
00:07:02.619 --> 00:07:03.359
Nice work.

227
00:07:03.989 --> 00:07:07.809
You might have noticed that we haven't added anything to waiting on yet,

228
00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:08.709
and don't worry,

229
00:07:08.829 --> 00:07:09.489
we'll get there.

230
00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:10.579
But before we do that,

231
00:07:10.769 --> 00:07:12.809
let's start by jumping into action items.

232
00:07:13.839 --> 00:07:14.989
Within action items,

233
00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:18.369
we can see the two different actions that we triaged here.

234
00:07:18.829 --> 00:07:22.029
I like breaking my action items into two different priorities,

235
00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.029
actions that I'll work on today,

236
00:07:24.309 --> 00:07:26.970
and all the actions that I'll work on later.

237
00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:32.049
Using pinning or flagging is a good way to separate all these different messages.

238
00:07:32.429 --> 00:07:32.549
Here,

239
00:07:32.589 --> 00:07:33.230
for example,

240
00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:34.989
I have that message from my manager,

241
00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:35.670
Patty,

242
00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:37.190
and given that she's my manager,

243
00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.630
this will probably be the most important task.

244
00:07:40.019 --> 00:07:40.170
Now,

245
00:07:40.179 --> 00:07:40.720
right over here,

246
00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:42.589
I could pin a message to the top,

247
00:07:42.619 --> 00:07:46.130
and that could denote that this needs to be completed as soon as possible.

248
00:07:46.339 --> 00:07:47.019
Alternatively,

249
00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.459
you can also flag a message.

250
00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.100
These are just different techniques that you could

251
00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:52.179
use to make messages stand out more.

252
00:07:52.299 --> 00:07:52.730
Now over here,

253
00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:53.859
I could turn off the flag,

254
00:07:54.019 --> 00:07:55.179
or I could turn off the pin,

255
00:07:55.339 --> 00:07:57.359
and then it looks like all the other messages.

256
00:07:57.779 --> 00:08:00.089
Once you go through and you complete one of the actions,

257
00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.640
and you respond to the question,

258
00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:02.579
right up on top,

259
00:08:02.679 --> 00:08:04.160
I recommend archiving the message.

260
00:08:04.459 --> 00:08:04.619
Here,

261
00:08:04.739 --> 00:08:05.570
I'll click on this,

262
00:08:05.739 --> 00:08:06.399
and now,

263
00:08:06.459 --> 00:08:08.179
Grady's ask has been completed.

264
00:08:08.779 --> 00:08:10.529
On closer inspection,

265
00:08:10.609 --> 00:08:14.970
it appears that Patty hasn't actually shared any of the updated packaging designs.

266
00:08:15.209 --> 00:08:17.609
So there's no way I could review or provide feedback.

267
00:08:17.809 --> 00:08:19.369
I should have caught that in my first response,

268
00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:20.850
but let me follow up again here,

269
00:08:20.929 --> 00:08:21.989
I'll click on reply,

270
00:08:22.209 --> 00:08:25.390
